  "query_preview": "..\n\nUpper ridging will help maintain mostly dry weather conditions\nacross the region for Friday into the weekend along with\nseasonable to slightly above normal temperatures. Low cloud and\npatchy fog have been included in near term grids given recent\nobservations as well as model trends. Better chances look to be\nacross southwest zones with light area winds, as well as in the\nriver valleys.\n\nMeanwhile, as the ridge axis shifts northeast, a new Pacific\ntrough will gain influence late in the weekend into early next\nweek. Southwest flow aloft in advance of the trough with an\napproaching shortwave will lead to increased rain chances late\nSunday as surface low across Wyoming tracks into the Dakotas.\nThese rain chances will continue into the early part of next week\nwith ensemble means around 0.25\" QPF.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was used for this forecast cycle with little in the way of\ndeviations. Confidence is below average on fog and stratus given\nlarge spread in placement among various models, but increasing\nconsensus is emerging with regard to precipitation chances Sunday\ninto Monday.",
